A||||5||FIEROCIOUS||How do you get burnt oil off of headers?||||5||
Z||000000||FIEROCIOUS||07-19-2000||09:06 PM||||I hot lashed my lifters today (what a F'n mess!) I used those little clippy thingy's to stop oil from going all over (didn't help)<BR>I have burnt oil resedue on my Fiero Store manifolds and it looks like crap! anyone had oil burn on their headers? <BR>how do you get it off without takeing the silver off? I tried carb cleaner it didn't work at all!<P>Someones had to have this problem.<BR>Thanks in advance.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||07-20-2000||12:59 AM||||Try WD40. I used it to clean off dried road tar and it worked great! It won't harm the finish. The only other thing I could think of would be Dupli-color grease and wax remover. This stuff won't harm the finish and I have used it to remove many year old brake dust stains from wheels.<BR>Let me know which one worked better.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIEROCIOUS||07-20-2000||01:53 AM||||You all are NOT going to belive what worked! first let me tell what I tried!<P>Carberator Cleaner= Didn't even work a little.<P>Water= Same as the carb cleaner.<P>Comet= Didn't scratch the headers or the burnt oil!<P>WD-40= made the oil stains real shiny but thats about it.<P>Adhesive remover= Great for adhesive no go on oil stains.<P>Asetone= Like water and everything else.<P>Gasoline= No good!<P>Solvent= Didn't even come close.<P>Oxyclean= NOPE!<P>Simple Green= Still not even a little scrubed off!<P>Fast Orange= Same as Comet. <P>Are you ready????<P>I was about to give up and my mother walked out and noticed the headers look like tarnished silverware so she went in the house got some TarnX and told me to try it! I realy didn't think this was going to work!<BR>I put some on a rag to humor her and it came off the instant I touched it to the oil stains! No shiz! I mean these headers were STAINED looked like old rusted stockies! Now they are all clean and shiney like the day I installed them!<P>So if you have a stuburn stain on your headers and tried everything go to your moms place and get some tarnX today!<P>I still can't belive it worked! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||07-20-2000||02:00 AM||||That is definately one to remember! (I have same manifolds!) Mom knows best I guess!||||reg||14
Z||000004||olympic||07-20-2000||02:13 AM||||  An old trick for hot lashing valves without making a mess is to take a set of old valve covers and cut it length wise down the top of the valve cover.  Then make small vertical cuts(perpendicular to the long cut) at each end of the valve cover.  Then bend the flaps up so they are vertical.  Now you have a custom fit splash gaurd that should eliminate most of the mess.<P>------------------<BR>"Born free....taxed to death."||||reg||1
Z||000005||FIEROCIOUS||07-20-2000||02:21 AM||||I use chev 350 valve covers for door stops but Fiero covers are kinda rare in these parts! Otherwise......||||reg||1
